    <string name="care_monstera_adansonii">The Monstera Adansonii, aka the \"Swiss Cheese\" plant, is an easy to care for plant that appreciates bright, indirect light. It is tolerant of medium to low light conditions, but prefers an east or west facing window.</string>
    <string name="care_jade_pothos">Jade Pothos is a fast-growing trailing plant with solid green, heart-shaped leaves. Water it when the top few centimetres of soil are dry and keep it in bright, indirect light, though it copes well with lower light too.</string>
    <string name="care_calathea_freddie">Calathea Freddie has long, light green leaves with dark green stripes that fold up at night. Keep the soil lightly moist, use filtered or rested water, and give it bright, indirect light and plenty of humidity.</string>
    <string name="care_calathea">Calatheas are called prayer plants because their patterned leaves move with the light during the day. They like evenly moist soil, high humidity and bright, indirect light; direct sun fades the leaves.</string>
    <string name="care_lancifolia">Calathea Lancifolia, the Rattlesnake Plant, has wavy, spotted leaves with purple undersides. Water when the top of the soil starts to dry, keep it away from cold drafts and out of direct sun.</string>
    <string name="care_monstera">Monstera Deliciosa grows large, split leaves as it matures. Let the top half of the soil dry out between waterings, give it bright, indirect light, and add a moss pole if you want it to climb.</string>
    <string name="care_pothos">Golden Pothos is one of the easiest houseplants to keep. Its marbled, heart-shaped leaves trail from shelves and baskets; water when the soil is half dry and keep it in medium to bright, indirect light.</string>

